Description: export the replicant factory symbols from the executable
 The Deskbar resolves this tray item by loading the provider image named
 in the archive's "add_on" string and looking up instantiate_deskbar_item
 and View::Instantiate(BMessage*). A plain executable keeps those symbols
 in .symtab only, which the loader cannot see, so the replicant would
 come back grey. Link with -rdynamic so the factory symbols reach the
 dynamic symbol table - the same export contract the tree's own
 replicant apps get from the runnable-add-on link rule, which the
 Makefile-Engine does not implement.
Author: Dario Casalinuovo <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -111,7 +111,7 @@
 COMPILER_FLAGS =
 
 #	Specify any additional linker flags to be used.
-LINKER_FLAGS =
+LINKER_FLAGS = -rdynamic
 
 #	Specify the version of this binary. Example:
 #		-app 3 4 0 d 0 -short 340 -long "340 "`echo -n -e '\302\251'`"1999 GNU GPL"
